// D984 — A SELF-REFERENTIAL MAP ARM, WITH NO `null` TO MASK IT. The declaration alone is
// the whole witness: no `is`, no binding, no value of type `T`. It used to TRAP THE
// COMPILER, which `vl check` never saw — check returned 0 and only `vl build` blew the
// wasm stack.
//
// `mvShapeOfMapNameArmTy` -> `mvShapeOfValNameArmTy` -> `mvValRowOfShape` is a
// three-function cycle that steps through `mapValNameOf` — the map's VALUE — and here that
// value is `T` again. Each lap EXPANDS the spelling rather than repeating it, so a
// name-keyed re-entry guard cannot see it; only a nesting bound can.
//
// The cycle steps through map values and NOT array elements, which is why
// `string | {[string]: T[]}` always ran. Mutual recursion through two maps trapped too, so
// both shapes are pinned here.
type T = string | {[string]: T}

type A = string | {[string]: B}

type B = string | {[string]: A}

type Arr = string | {[string]: Arr[]}

print("ok")

print("ok")

